 Our contributions are threefold:
 \begin{itemize}
-\item We formulate client-aware target-matrix selection for resource-constrained federated fine-tuning, making the trainable projection subset responsive to local data and device feasibility rather than specifying it solely through adapter capacity.
-\item We develop FedMATRIX-LoRA, which connects local gradient-based profiling with feasible configuration generation and server coordination. The framework supports distinct projection choices within a Transformer block and across clients while maintaining a shared global adapter through matrix-wise aggregation.
-\item We provide a conditional stationarity analysis that relates selective aggregation to effective-update bias and matrix coverage, and evaluate the complete framework on image classification, language understanding, and dialogue summarization under heterogeneous data and analytical resource profiles.
+\item We formulate importance-guided target-matrix selection for resource-constrained federated fine-tuning, allowing projections within a Transformer block to be selected independently. A matched-budget controlled study motivates this granularity using actual short-term adaptation gains under both local and server-proxy scoring.
+\item We develop FedMATRIX-LoRA to connect local matrix profiling with resource-feasible configuration generation, shared-budget coordination, and matrix-wise aggregation. Clients can update distinct target subsets while contributing to a common global adapter.
+\item We provide a conditional stationarity analysis of selective aggregation and evaluate the framework across image classification, language understanding, and dialogue summarization. Controlled scoring and ablation studies examine the mechanisms separately from the complete system's performance.
 \end{itemize}
 
